<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Sail</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>sail &lt;direction&gt;
</pre>
<p>Example:
</p>
<pre>sail east
</pre>
<p>Deep water, a lake or the sea, can't be waded or swum: you need a boat. 
Shallow water you can swim instead (see <a cmd='#'>Help Swimming</a>).
</p><p>To sail, drop your boat by the water, enter it (see <a cmd='#'>Help Enter</a>), and 
sail the way you want to go: the boat carries you, and anything aboard, 
across the water. While you sit in the boat, sail east does the same as 
just east. Leave the boat when you reach the far shore, and take it with 
you if you will need it again.
</p><p>Boats are sold at the boat shop in Midgaard (see <a cmd='#'>Help Midgaard</a>), among 
other places.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Swimming</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Enter</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Movement</a>
</pre>




</div>